<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19135" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fuscĭna</span></b> , ae, f.
		kindr. with furca, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a three-pronged spear</i>, <i>a
				trident</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dant (deo) arcum, sagittas, hastam, clipeum,
					fuscinam, fulmen,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D. 1, 36, 101</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">as an attribute of Neptune,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Calig. 52</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">as a weapon of the retiarii,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 30</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Juv. 2, 143</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Paul. Sent. 3, 6, 66</span></i>.</div>
